Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:54:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] WIP: arm64: dts: qcom: sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246:
 Shrink the WLAN MSA region
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The SoC's memory map reserves 12 MiB at 0x82a00000 for the WLAN, which
is what a WCN6750 needs. This phone pairs the Adrastea core with a
WCN3990-class radio, and Sony's device tree shrinks the region to
3 MiB for it. ath10k hands that size to the firmware as the MSA, so
use the same.

To be folded into the SM6450 DT / board DT once it has probed on the device.

Signed-off-by: Bruno Gregório <accounts@bruno.pw>
---
 .../boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts     | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts
index 77fb96890..4514bcbcc 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6450-sony-xperia-columbia-pdx246.dts
@@ -395,6 +395,11 @@ &mdss_dsi0_phy {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&pil_wlan_mem {
+	/* The WCN3990's MSA; the SoC's map leaves room for a larger WLAN */
+	reg = <0x0 0x82a00000 0x0 0x300000>;
+};
+
 &pm6150l_gpios {
 	panel_vddio_en: panel-vddio-en-state {
 		pins = "gpio9";
